hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"344","A chapter on showing favor to offspring: Musaddad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu al-Safar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr: Whoever captures Umm Hakim ibn Hizam, let him release her. A man of the Ansar had captured her by her braid; when he heard the caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he released her."
